# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
# `.vscode/*` and not `.vscode/`: git will not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# negation cannot re-include anything inside one. Excluding the contents leaves the
# directory readable and the exception below effective.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/

# Node (for the future generator/tooling)
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Session-scoped working files — carry one session to the next, never committed.
# Anchored to the root: a bare `HANDOFF.md` also matches templates/handoff.md, which is a
# shipped artifact and must be committed.
/HANDOFF.md
.arc-work/
.timescope/

# The live event log — m44. Every hook firing appends to it, so a tracked copy leaves every
# worktree dirty at every moment and one `git add -u` sweeps thousands of machine-written
# lines into a review diff. #273. The record is not lost by ignoring it: rotation at arc close
# moves the file to `docs/arc-log/events/`, which IS tracked, and that move is the one
# deliberate step that commits an arc's events — templates/event-log.md, § Rotation.
# Anchored at the root: the path is the one `hooks/lib/activation-log` writes, and a bare
# `log.md` would match any file of that name anywhere in the repository.
/.claude/arc/log.md

# `.arc-work/archive/` above also covers the recovery copies `hooks/handoff-archive` takes
# before a user-authored file is replaced — #152. Recovery, not record: it must stay ignored,
# or the record grows a stale copy of every handoff the arc ever had.
